==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|þrír|lang=is}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|þrīz|lang=gem-pro}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|tréyes|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Faroese ''[[tríggir]]'', Norwegian, Swedish, and Danish {{term|tre|lang=da}}.

===Cardinal number===
'''þrír''' {{m-p}}, '''[[þrjár]]''' {{f-p}}, '''[[þrjú]]''' {{n-p}}

# '''[[three]]'''; the cardinal number after [[tveir#Icelandic|tveir]] and before [[fjórir#Icelandic|fjórir]].

